<div id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5.2.3 Impact of Aggregation and Probing Classier ‣ 5.2 Intrinsic Analysis ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Model-Agnostic Correctness Assessment for LLM-Generated Code via Dynamic Internal Representation Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> presents the performance of <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AutoProbe</span> with different <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">aggregation functions</span>, which are applied to combine the weighted representations in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> before feeding them to a probing classifier (Sec. <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Code Correctness Predictor ‣ 3 Model-Agnostic Correctness Assessment for LLM-Generated Code via Dynamic Internal Representation Selection ‣ Model-Agnostic Correctness Assessment for LLM-Generated Code via Dynamic Internal Representation Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>).
Among the evaluated strategies, <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">max pooling proves to be the most effective aggregation function, enabling <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AutoProbe</span> to achieve the highest prediction performance.</span>
As seen, with <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">max pooling</span>, <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AutoProbe</span> achieves an accuracy of 0.79, which is about 10% higher than the worst setting using <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">min pooling</span>.
This indicates that <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">max pooling</span>, by selecting the most prominent features across representation dimensions, captures more discriminative signals for code correctness prediction, thereby enhancing <span id="S5.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AutoProbe</span>’s overall performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="S5.T9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of Probing Classifiers on <span id="S5.T9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AutoProbe</span>’s Performance</span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T9.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:57.4pt;vertical-align:-25.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(24.6pt,-4.1pt) scale(1.1665243976526,1.1665243976526) ;">
